            <h1>🌿 Peaty and Marshy Soil – Full Information</h1>
            <br>

            <h2>✅ What is Peaty and Marshy Soil?</h2>

            <p>
                Peaty and marshy soil is a type of soil that forms in water-logged and swampy areas.
                It contains a large amount of organic matter (dead plants and animals), which makes
                it dark and rich.
            </p>

            <br>

            <b>📍 Where is it Found in India?</b>
            <p>
                This soil is mainly found in areas with heavy rainfall and high humidity.
            </p>

            <b>👉 Major regions:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Kerala (most common)</li>
                <li>West Bengal (Sundarbans area)</li>
                <li>Odisha coastal regions</li>
                <li>Tamil Nadu coastal areas</li>
                <li>Parts of Bihar and Uttar Pradesh</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🎨 Colour and Appearance</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Usually dark brown or black</li>
                <li>Soft and spongy texture</li>
                <li>Contains partially decomposed plant material</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🧪 Composition</b>
            <ul>
                <li>High organic matter (humus)</li>
                <li>Large amount of moisture</li>
                <li>Acidic nature</li>
                <li>Low mineral nutrients like potash and phosphate</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🌧️ Formation</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Plants grow in swampy areas</li>
                <li>Due to excess water, plants do not fully decompose</li>
                <li>Organic matter accumulates over time</li>
                <li>Soil becomes rich in peat (decayed vegetation)</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🌾 Fertility</b>

            <p><b>👉 Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Rich in organic content</li>
                <li>Good moisture retention</li>
                <li>Supports certain crops well</li>
            </ul>

            <p><b>👉 Disadvantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Too acidic</li>
                <li>Poor drainage</li>
                <li>Low availability of some nutrients</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🌱 Crops Grown in Peaty and Marshy Soil</b>
            <p>This soil is suitable mainly for water-loving crops:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Paddy (Rice)</li>
                <li>Jute</li>
                <li>Coconut</li>
                <li>Some vegetables and grasses</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>💧 Water Holding Capacity</b>
            <ol>
                <li>Very high</li>
                <li>Remains wet most of the time</li>
                <li>Sometimes causes waterlogging problems</li>
            </ol>

            <br>

            <b>⚠️ Problems with This Soil</b>
            <ol>
                <li>Excess moisture</li>
                <li>Acidic nature affects crop growth</li>
                <li>Needs proper drainage system</li>
                <li>Requires fertilizers and lime treatment</li>
            </ol>

            <br>

            <b>🛠️ Improvement Methods</b>
            <p>Farmers improve this soil by:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Providing drainage channels</li>
                <li>Adding lime to reduce acidity</li>
                <li>Using fertilizers to increase nutrients</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🧠 Easy Memory Trick</b>
            <p>👉 Peaty = Plants + Water + Organic matter</p>

        </section>

    </div>

</div>

